        "item": "thm-smooth-functions-defined-locally-can-be-glued-by-a-partition-of-unity",
        "finding": "Proof 3.1 says: “If φ_i(p)=0, then p∉supp(φ_i)”. Vanishing does not imply exclusion from the closed support: a smooth nonnegative bump vanishes at a boundary point of its support. The theorem remains supported by Step 1.1 and support containment in U_i, which give F_i(p)=0 even at such points. This is an immediately closable proof error, not a false smooth-gluing theorem.",
